{"id":"mahabharata-3-046","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":46,"title":"षट्चत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 46 · Dhritarashtra's dread of Arjuna","summary":{"en":"Hearing of Arjuna's feats in heaven, Dhritarashtra tells Sanjaya of his fear: Arjuna armed with divine weapons, Bhima burning for revenge and Krishna at their side will leave none of his sons alive. Sanjaya agrees that the Pandavas will not forget their wrongs.","kn":"ಸ್ವರ್ಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಸಾಧನೆಗಳನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿ ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನು ತನ್ನ ಭಯವನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ: ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರಧಾರಿ ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಸೇಡಿಗಾಗಿ ಉರಿಯುವ ಭೀಮ, ಜೊತೆಗಿರುವ ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣರು ತನ್ನ ಮಕ್ಕಳಲ್ಲಿ ಯಾರನ್ನೂ ಉಳಿಸರು. ಪಾಂಡವರು ತಮಗಾದ ಅನ್ಯಾಯ ಮರೆಯರು ಎಂದು ಸಂಜಯನು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"स्वर्ग में अर्जुन के पराक्रम सुनकर धृतराष्ट्र संजय से अपना भय कहते हैं: दिव्यास्त्रधारी अर्जुन, बदले की आग में जलते भीम और साथ खड़े श्रीकृष्ण उनके किसी पुत्र को जीवित नहीं छोड़ेंगे। संजय सहमत हैं कि पाण्डव अपने साथ हुए अन्याय को नहीं भूलेंगे।","te":"స్వర్గంలో అర్జునుని ఘనతలు విని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు సంజయునితో తన భయాన్ని చెబుతాడు: దివ్యాస్త్రధారి అర్జునుడు, ప్రతీకారంతో రగిలే భీముడు, వారి పక్కన ఉన్న శ్రీకృష్ణుడు తన కుమారులలో ఎవరినీ మిగల్చరు. పాండవులు తమకు జరిగిన అన్యాయాన్ని మరువరని సంజయుడు అంగీకరిస్తాడు.","ta":"ஸ்வர்க்கத்தில் அர்ஜுனனின் சாதனைகளைக் கேட்டுத் திருதராஷ்டிரன் தன் அச்சத்தை ஸஞ்ஜயனிடம் சொல்கிறான்: தெய்வீக அஸ்திரங்கள் ஏந்திய அர்ஜுனன், பழிவாங்க எரியும் பீமன், உடனிருக்கும் ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் தன் மைந்தர்களில் எவரையும் உயிருடன் விடமாட்டார்கள். பாண்டவர்கள் தமக்கு நேர்ந்த அநீதியை மறக்கமாட்டார்கள் என்று ஸஞ்ஜயன் ஒப்புகிறான்.","ml":"സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിലെ അർജുനന്റെ പരാക്രമങ്ങൾ കേട്ട് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രൻ സഞ്ജയനോട് തന്റെ ഭയം പറയുന്നു: ദിവ്യാസ്ത്രങ്ങളുള്ള അർജുനൻ, പ്രതികാരാഗ്നിയിൽ എരിയുന്ന ഭീമൻ, അവർക്കൊപ്പം കൃഷ്ണൻ എന്നിവർ തന്റെ പുത്രന്മാരിൽ ആരെയും ജീവനോടെ വിടില്ല. പാണ്ഡവർ തങ്ങളോടുള്ള അനീതി മറക്കില്ലെന്ന് സഞ്ജയൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.46; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"इन्द्रलोकाभिगमनपर्व","titleEn":"Indralokabhigamana Parva (Journey to Indra's world)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अत्यद्भुतमिदं कर्म पार्थस्यामिततेजसः ।\nधृतराष्ट्रो महातेजाः श्रुत्वा विप्र किमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Holy sage, the deed of Partha of boundless splendor is wondrous indeed. What did the mighty Dhritarashtra say when he heard of it?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"शक्रलोकगतं पार्थं श्रुत्वा राजाम्बिकासुतः ।\nद्वैपायनादृषिश्रेष्ठात्संजयं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the son of Ambika heard that Partha had gone to the world of Indra, he spoke to Sanjaya, having heard of it from the best of sages, Dvaipayana."}},{"n":3,"text":"श्रुतं मे सूत कार्त्स्न्येन कर्म पार्थस्य धीमतः ।\nकच्चित्तवापि विदितं यथातथ्येन सारथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said: Charioteer, I have heard in full the deeds of wise Partha. Perhaps you too know exactly how things stand."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रमत्तो ग्राम्यधर्मेषु मन्दात्मा पापनिश्चयः ।\nमम पुत्रः सुदुर्बुद्धिः पृथिवीं घातयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My son, heedless in worldly pleasures, dull-minded, set on wrong, and of very bad judgment, will bring about the slaughter of the earth."}},{"n":5,"text":"यस्य नित्यमृता वाचः स्वैरेष्वपि महात्मनः ।\nत्रैलोक्यमपि तस्य स्याद्योद्धा यस्य धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The man whose very jests are always true, whose warrior is Dhananjaya, could face even the three worlds as a fighter."}},{"n":6,"text":"अस्यतः कर्णिनाराचांस्तीक्ष्णाग्रांश्च शिलाशितान् ।\nकोऽर्जुनस्याग्रतस्तिष्ठेदपि मृत्युर्जरातिगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Arjuna looses his barbed arrows and sharp stone-whetted iron shafts, who could stand before him, even Death who is beyond old age?"}},{"n":7,"text":"मम पुत्रा दुरात्मानः सर्वे मृत्युवशं गताः ।\nयेषां युद्धं दुराधर्षैः पाण्डवैः प्रत्युपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All my wicked sons have come under the power of death, for war has come upon them against the unassailable Pandavas."}},{"n":8,"text":"तस्यैव च न पश्यामि युधि गाण्डीवधन्वनः ।\nअनिशं चिन्तयानोऽपि य एनमुदियाद्रथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though I think of it constantly, I see no chariot-warrior in battle who could rise up against that wielder of the Gandiva."}},{"n":9,"text":"द्रोणकर्णौ प्रतीयातां यदि भीष्मोऽपि वा रणे ।\nमहान्स्यात्संशयो लोके न तु पश्यामि नो जयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If Drona and Karna should face him in battle, or even Bhishma, the world would be in great doubt, yet I do not see victory for us."}},{"n":10,"text":"घृणी कर्णः प्रमादी च आचार्यः स्थविरो गुरुः ।\nअमर्षी बलवान्पार्थः संरम्भी दृढविक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna is soft-hearted and careless, the teacher is old and revered, while Partha is wrathful, strong, furious and firm in prowess."}},{"n":11,"text":"भवेत्सुतुमुलं युद्धं सर्वशोऽप्यपराजितम् ।\nसर्वे ह्यस्त्रविदः शूराः सर्वे प्राप्ता महद्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The battle would be a terrible uproar, undefeated on every side, for all are brave and skilled in weapons, and all have won great fame."}},{"n":12,"text":"अपि सर्वेश्वरत्वं हि न वाञ्छेरन्पराजिताः ।\nवधे नूनं भवेच्छान्तिस्तेषां वा फल्गुनस्य वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if defeated they would not want lordship over all; surely peace will come only through the death of them or of Phalguna."}},{"n":13,"text":"न तु हन्तार्जुनस्यास्ति जेता वास्य न विद्यते ।\nमन्युस्तस्य कथं शाम्येन्मन्दान्प्रति समुत्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Arjuna has no slayer and no conqueror. How will his wrath, roused against my dull sons, ever be calmed?"}},{"n":14,"text":"त्रिदशेशसमो वीरः खाण्डवेऽग्निमतर्पयत् ।\nजिगाय पार्थिवान्सर्वान्राजसूये महाक्रतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hero, equal to the lord of the gods, fed Agni at Khandava and defeated all the kings at the great Rajasuya sacrifice."}},{"n":15,"text":"शेषं कुर्याद्गिरेर्वज्रं निपतन्मूर्ध्नि संजय ।\nन तु कुर्युः शराः शेषमस्तास्तात किरीटिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, a thunderbolt falling on a mountain's peak might leave something of it, but arrows shot by the diadem-wearer would leave nothing."}},{"n":16,"text":"यथा हि किरणा भानोस्तपन्तीह चराचरम् ।\nतथा पार्थभुजोत्सृष्टाः शरास्तप्स्यन्ति मे सुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sun's rays scorch all moving and unmoving things here, so the arrows loosed from Partha's arms will scorch my sons."}},{"n":17,"text":"अपि वा रथघोषेण भयार्ता सव्यसाचिनः ।\nप्रतिभाति विदीर्णेव सर्वतो भारती चमूः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the rumble of Savyasachin's chariot, I imagine the Bharata army, stricken with fear, seems split apart on every side."}},{"n":18,"text":"यदुद्वपन्प्रवपंश्चैव बाणा-\nन्स्थाताततायी समरे किरीटी ।\nसृष्टोऽन्तकः सर्वहरो विधात्रा\nभवेद्यथा तद्वदपारणीयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the diadem-wearer stands in battle as an attacker, drawing and showering arrows, he will be as unstoppable as Death, creator of all, whom the Ordainer sent forth to take everything."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"यदेतत्कथितं राजंस्त्वया दुर्योधनं प्रति ।\nसर्वमेतद्यथात्थ त्वं नैतन्मिथ्या महीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, all that you have said about Duryodhana is as you say it; none of it is false, lord of the earth."}},{"n":20,"text":"मन्युना हि समाविष्टाः पाण्डवास्तेऽमितौजसः ।\nदृष्ट्वा कृष्णां सभां नीतां धर्मपत्नीं यशस्विनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas of immeasurable might are filled with fury, having seen the glorious Krishna, their lawful wife, dragged into the assembly."}},{"n":21,"text":"दुःशासनस्य ता वाचः श्रुत्वा ते दारुणोदयाः ।\nकर्णस्य च महाराज न स्वप्स्यन्तीति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I believe that having heard the words of Duhshasana and Karna, those men of terrible resolve will not sleep."}},{"n":22,"text":"श्रुतं हि ते महाराज यथा पार्थेन संयुगे ।\nएकादशतनुः स्थाणुर्धनुषा परितोषितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O great king, you have heard how Sthanu, the eleven-bodied god, was pleased by Partha in combat."}},{"n":23,"text":"कैरातं वेषमास्थाय योधयामास फल्गुनम् ।\nजिज्ञासुः सर्वदेवेशः कपर्दी भगवान्स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the form of a Kirata, the blessed lord of all gods, the matted-haired one himself, fought Phalguna out of a wish to test him."}},{"n":24,"text":"तत्रैनं लोकपालास्ते दर्शयामासुरर्जुनम् ।\nअस्त्रहेतोः पराक्रान्तं तपसा कौरवर्षभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the guardians of the world revealed themselves to Arjuna, that bull of the Kurus who strove with austerity for weapons."}},{"n":25,"text":"नैतदुत्सहतेऽन्यो हि लब्धुमन्यत्र फल्गुनात् ।\nसाक्षाद्दर्शनमेतेषामीश्वराणां नरो भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"No other man on earth could hope to gain a direct vision of these lords, except Phalguna."}},{"n":26,"text":"महेश्वरेण यो राजन्न जीर्णो ग्रस्तमूर्तिमान् ।\nकस्तमुत्सहते वीरं युद्धे जरयितुं पुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Who among men would dare to wear down in battle the hero whom Mahadeva himself, embodied, could not exhaust, O king?"}},{"n":27,"text":"आसादितमिदं घोरं तुमुलं लोमहर्षणम् ।\nद्रौपदीं परिकर्षद्भिः कोपयद्भिश्च पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This dreadful, tumultuous, hair-raising thing has been brought about by those who dragged Draupadi and enraged the Pandavas."}},{"n":28,"text":"यत्र विस्फुरमाणोष्ठो भीमः प्राह वचो महत् ।\nदृष्ट्वा दुर्योधनेनोरू द्रौपद्या दर्शितावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Bhima, lips quivering, spoke mighty words when Duryodhana showed both his thighs to Draupadi."}},{"n":29,"text":"ऊरू भेत्स्यामि ते पाप गदया वज्रकल्पया ।\nत्रयोदशानां वर्षाणामन्ते दुर्द्यूतदेविनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Wicked one, at the end of the thirteen years I will break your thighs with my mace like a thunderbolt, you gambler at foul dice.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"सर्वे प्रहरतां श्रेष्ठाः सर्वे चामिततेजसः ।\nसर्वे सर्वास्त्रविद्वांसो देवैरपि सुदुर्जयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them are the best of fighters, all of boundless splendor, all masters of every weapon, hard to conquer even for gods."}},{"n":31,"text":"मन्ये मन्युसमुद्धूताः पुत्राणां तव संयुगे ।\nअन्तं पार्थाः करिष्यन्ति वीर्यामर्षसमन्विताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think the sons of Pritha, roused by rage and full of valor and anger, will bring your sons to their end in battle."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"किं कृतं सूत कर्णेन वदता परुषं वचः ।\nपर्याप्तं वैरमेतावद्यत्कृष्णा सा सभां गता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, what did Karna do by speaking harsh words? Enough enmity had already arisen when Krishna was brought into the assembly."}},{"n":33,"text":"अपीदानीं मम सुतास्तिष्ठेरन्मन्दचेतसः ।\nयेषां भ्राता गुरुर्ज्येष्ठो विनये नावतिष्ठते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Would my foolish sons even survive now, when their eldest brother, their elder and teacher, does not stand in good conduct?"}},{"n":34,"text":"ममापि वचनं सूत न शुश्रूषति मन्दभाक् ।\nदृष्ट्वा मां चक्षुषा हीनं निर्विचेष्टमचेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The unlucky fool does not listen even to me, though he sees me blind, helpless and bereft of sense."}},{"n":35,"text":"ये चास्य सचिवा मन्दाः कर्णसौबलकादयः ।\nतेऽप्यस्य भूयसो दोषान्वर्धयन्ति विचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His dull counselors, Karna, Saubala and the rest, in their folly only heap more faults upon him."}},{"n":36,"text":"स्वैरमुक्ता अपि शराः पार्थेनामिततेजसा ।\nनिर्दहेयुर्मम सुतान्किं पुनर्मन्युनेरिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even arrows loosed carelessly by Partha of boundless splendor would burn my sons; what then when sped by anger?"}},{"n":37,"text":"पार्थबाहुबलोत्सृष्टा महाचापविनिःसृताः ।\nदिव्यास्त्रमन्त्रमुदिताः सादयेयुः सुरानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sent by the strength of Partha's arms from his great bow, charged with mantras of divine weapons, they could strike down even gods."}},{"n":38,"text":"यस्य मन्त्री च गोप्ता च सुहृच्चैव जनार्दनः ।\nहरिस्त्रैलोक्यनाथः स किं नु तस्य न निर्जितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The man whose counselor, protector and friend is Janardana, Hari, lord of the three worlds, what is there that he has not conquered?"}},{"n":39,"text":"इदं च सुमहच्चित्रमर्जुनस्येह संजय ।\nमहादेवेन बाहुभ्यां यत्समेत इति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And this too is a great wonder concerning Arjuna, Sanjaya: they say he grappled with Mahadeva arm to arm."}},{"n":40,"text":"प्रत्यक्षं सर्वलोकस्य खाण्डवे यत्कृतं पुरा ।\nफल्गुनेन सहायार्थे वह्नेर्दामोदरेण च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Before all the world's eyes, Phalguna and Damodara earlier did what they did at Khandava to help the god of fire."}},{"n":41,"text":"सर्वथा नास्ति मे पुत्रः सामात्यः सहबान्धवः ।\nक्रुद्धे पार्थे च भीमे च वासुदेवे च सात्वते ॥","meaning":{"en":"In every way my son, with his ministers and kinsmen, is lost once Partha, Bhima and Vasudeva of the Satvatas are angry."}}]}]}